MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The USB 3.0 extension cables fit my previous use of USB extensions and my current interest in making desk devices easier to connect and reach.",
    "The external drive enclosure felt useful because it could let me connect a spare laptop drive through USB, provided the drive fits. That practical connection task appeals to me more than an internal upgrade."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The internal SSDs, desktop hard drive, CPU cooler, and power adapters assume an upgrade or repair project that I do not currently have.",
    "Another HDMI cable or a USB-B cable would only help if I needed that particular connection or extra length. Owning related cables does not mean I need replacements now."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in computer accessories seems to have been stretched into an interest in building or upgrading a desktop.",
    "My previous cable purchases seem to have been treated as a continuing need for more cables, without enough attention to the connector and purpose."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent purchases suggest practical setup tasks such as connecting devices, organizing my desk, and maintaining equipment. A clear everyday use matters more to me than a broad connection to computers.",
    "Similar products can satisfy the same need: both USB extension packs appeal to me, but I would choose one. Internal parts also need a specific compatible machine and a concrete reason to upgrade."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my interest in useful connection accessories but assumed more demand for internal upgrades and additional cables than I currently have."
}
